- Register custom post types and taxonomies using `register_post_type` and `register_taxonomy`.
- Prefix all custom post type and taxonomy slugs.
- Document and register shortcodes with clear usage and sanitization.
- Build widgets using `WP_Widget` and follow WordPress widget API.
- Ensure plugins/themes are compatible with multisite installations.
- Add WP-CLI commands for advanced plugin/theme management.

## Examples

```php
// Register a custom post type
add_action( 'init', function() {
    register_post_type( 'myplugin_book', array(
        'label' => __( 'Books', 'my-plugin' ),
        'public' => true,
        'supports' => array( 'title', 'editor', 'thumbnail' ),
    ));
});
```

```php
// Register a shortcode
add_shortcode( 'myplugin_hello', function( $atts ) {
    $atts = shortcode_atts( array( 'name' => 'World' ), $atts, 'myplugin_hello' );
    return 'Hello, ' . esc_html( $atts['name'] ) . '!';
});
```

```php
// WP-CLI command
if ( defined( 'WP_CLI' ) && WP_CLI ) {
    WP_CLI::add_command( 'myplugin greet', function( $args ) {
        WP_CLI::success( 'Hello from MyPlugin!' );
    });
}
```

